cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Above 4G Decoding unlock: enabling a hidden 64-bit PCIe MMIO window on OEM UEFI boards"
abstract: >-
  Documentation and guarded tools for enabling Above 4G Decoding / Above 4GB MMIO on OEM UEFI boards that
  ship the option but hide it, so a large-BAR GPU can boot instead of failing with "PCI Out of Resources".
  The method edits the board's own UEFI setup variables with a backup first, dry-run by default, refusal
  of any wrong-size or protected write, and a live measurement of vendor checksum guards. Reference build:
  Lenovo ThinkCentre M720q Tiny with a 16 GB NVIDIA A2.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: dmmdea
repository-code: "https://github.com/dmmdea/above-4g-decoding-unlock"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Above 4G Decoding
  - PCIe BAR
  - MMIO
  - UEFI variables
  - efivarfs
  - OEM firmware
  - hardware reuse
